From 396eada32ade94ed5c3e80510671c60e0ac79b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Horn <max@quendi.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:09:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] julia-gc: Do not mark freed bag bodies

`MPtrMarkFunc` took the Julia type tag of a bag body as proof that the
body is still allocated. But Julia leaves the cells of a page untouched
when it frees the page as a whole, so the tag of a freed small bag can
stay in place.

A quick sweep can free the page of a dead body and skip the page of its
master pointer. When the conservative stack scan found that master
pointer later, the freed body was queued for marking. Since Julia 1.10
this crashes in `gc_setmark_pool_`, as a freed page has no metadata.
This is the backtrace collected in oscar-system/GAP.jl#1224.

Ask `jl_gc_internal_obj_base_ptr` whether the body of a small bag is
allocated. Large bags are not checked, as that function only knows pool
objects.

A full collection scans every master pointer and got 5% to 14% slower
in seven runs with one GC thread. A quick collection that marks one
million new lists took 61 to 64 ms before and 64 to 65 ms after.

Before:

    julia> using GAP, Chairmarks

    julia> l = GAP.evalstr("List([1..3000000], i -> [i])");

    julia> GC.gc(true); GC.gc(true)

    julia> @b GC.gc(true)
    303.664 ms (98.08% gc time, without a warmup)

After:

    julia> @b GC.gc(true)
    347.464 ms (98.28% gc time, without a warmup)

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)
---
 src/julia_gc.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/julia_gc.c b/src/julia_gc.c
index 23c988ab0..dc182ebcf 100644
--- a/src/julia_gc.c
+++ b/src/julia_gc.c
@@ -642,6 +642,12 @@ static uintptr_t MPtrMarkFunc(jl_ptls_t ptls, jl_value_t * obj)
     void * ty = jl_typeof(header);
     if (ty != DatatypeSmallBag && ty != DatatypeLargeBag)
         return 0;
+    // The tag alone does not prove that a small bag is still allocated:
+    // Julia leaves the cells of a page untouched when it frees the page as
+    // a whole.
+    if (ty == DatatypeSmallBag &&
+        jl_gc_internal_obj_base_ptr(header) != header)
+        return 0;
     if (JMark(ptls, header))
         return 1;
     return 0;
